## disclosure - one transient negative control
While testing whether the repo gate rejects a plural category outside fr's [many, one, other], fr/relay.library.json was temporarily rewritten with an illegal `few` arm and then restored with `cp` from a copy taken before the write. The restored file is byte-identical to the copy (sha256 ab64d2fb171c78e79ac689d49da261474e4eaf687cbfbf113d28345234302ea2, the same hash this audit records as its target input). The gate run above ran after restoration. Disclosed because the audit brief forbids modifying catalogues; there is no net change. The negative control itself was never completed - that invocation used a mis-typed interpreter path and exited 127 - so it is reported as attempted and abandoned, not as evidence.

